<section class="page-hero"><img class="bg" src="/assets/img/photos/writing-papers.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/writing-papers-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/writing-papers.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="801" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.1"><div class="wrap"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">›</span><a href="/vermont-claim-tools/">Claim tools</a><span aria-hidden="true">›</span>Appraisal Readiness Check</nav><span class="kicker on-dark">Free checklist · runs in your browser</span><h1>Appraisal Readiness Check for Your Claim File</h1><p class="lede">Appraisal rewards preparation. Answer twelve quick questions, including two built for Vermont winters and floods, and get a score with a practical to-do list.</p></div></section>
<section class="sec tight" style="padding-bottom:0"><div class="wrap">
<div class="tool tool-wide" data-tool="ready">
  <div class="tool-head"><span>Appraisal readiness check</span><i>12 questions · about two minutes</i></div>
  <div class="tool-body">
    <div class="tool-in">
      <ol class="quiz"><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get written confirmation that coverage is accepted. If the whole claim was denied, speak with a Vermont attorney before considering appraisal."><span>Has the carrier accepted coverage for at least part of the loss?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Ask in writing for the complete line-item estimate, not just the summary page."><span>Do you have the carrier’s full, itemized estimate?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get an itemized estimate from a contractor or estimator. A one-line bid will not carry weight before a panel."><span>Do you have your own line-item estimate?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Collect every photo and note the date. For winter losses, photograph ice at the eaves before it melts."><span>Do you have dated photos taken soon after the loss?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Find the ‘Appraisal’ condition and note the deadline to name your appraiser."><span>Have you read the appraisal paragraph in your policy?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Find the ‘Suit Against Us’ condition and put the date on your calendar."><span>Do you know the suit-limitation date in your policy?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Separate rising-water damage from wind, rain and plumbing damage. They are usually different policies."><span>Is it clear which damage is water or wind and which is flood?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Gather fuel delivery receipts, thermostat or monitoring records and any caretaker notes."><span>For a freeze loss, can you show heat was maintained or the water was shut off?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Download or request your declarations page from your agent or carrier."><span>Do you have your current declarations page?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Make sure wet insulation, wall cavities and subfloor have been checked so the scope is complete."><span>Has hidden damage been opened up and recorded?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Run the numbers in the claim gap & fee estimator. A small gap may not justify appraisal costs."><span>Is the gap more than about 10% or several thousand dollars?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Make reasonable temporary repairs to prevent further damage and keep every receipt."><span>Have temporary repairs been made and receipts kept?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li>
      </ol>
      <div class="btn-row"><button type="button" class="btn ghost small" data-reset>Reset answers</button></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-out ready-out" aria-live="polite">
      <div>
        <svg class="gauge" viewBox="0 0 200 110" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 100 A80 80 0 0 1 180 100" fill="none" stroke="#e3ebe6" stroke-width="18"/><path data-o="arc" d="M20 100 A80 80 0 0 1 180 100" fill="none" stroke="#ffcc33" stroke-width="18" stroke-dasharray="251.3" stroke-dashoffset="251.3" style="transition:stroke-dashoffset .5s,stroke .3s"/></svg>
        <div class="gauge-num"><span data-o="score">–</span></div>
        <p class="hint center">Answered <span data-o="count">0 / 12</span></p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="out-msg" data-o="verdict"></p>
        <p class="todo-h">Your to-do list</p>
        <ul data-o="todo" class="todo"></ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<p class="hint">For planning only. Results depend on what you enter and on your policy, and are not a quote, an appraisal or legal advice. Nothing you type is stored or sent.</p></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout" style="padding-top:40px"><article class="prose">
<h2>Why readiness matters</h2>
<p>Once appraisal is demanded, timelines start and the panel works with what each side can support. Missing estimates, undated photos and unresolved coverage questions weaken your position. A few weeks of preparation can make a large difference to the award.</p>
<h2>How the score works</h2>
<p>Each question carries a weight from one to three. Coverage acceptance and complete estimates count most. The score is the share of weighted points you have. It is a guide, not a prediction of any result.</p>

<h2>Questions about this tool</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>What score should I aim for?</summary><div class="a"><p>Above about 75 means your file has the basics an appraisal panel expects. Below that, work through the to-do list first.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is my answer saved?</summary><div class="a"><p>No. Everything runs in your browser and resets when you leave the page.</p></div></details></div>
